Q1 Project Awards.reason:
EU Product Initialization Project Team
Background: EU is one of the key markets for Full Service business with complex compliance requirements. During EU market launch preparation, Full Service needed to drive product and seller product EU compliance transformation, with a target of 400,000 sellable products before launch. Project complexity manifested in:
- Multiple stakeholders: Involving FS industry, B/C-end products, GS GNE, EMEA GNE, compliance, regional/headquarters legal, requiring alignment with multiple FS internal and external teams;
- Insufficient seller attention: Unable to communicate accurate EU launch timeline to sellers early on; combined with relatively new regulatory requirements, sellers had high comprehension costs and perceived significant upfront investment, generally preferring to prioritize US/UK markets;
- Complex compliance requirements: Including EPR qualification preparation, EU responsible person/manufacturer information, category qualifications, product attributes, etc. Requirements are complex with long preparation times, requiring clear and accurate communication of platform requirements from product design, operation tutorials, and training course perspectives.

Outstanding results:
Against this backdrop, the project team ultimately achieved 640K products with uploaded qualifications, 550K reviewed products, and 470K successfully listed products, exceeding targets.

Implementation path:
- Promoted tax withholding capability building: Initiated research on sellers and competitor platforms, determined that competitor platforms had complete tax withholding functionality and most sellers chose to use platform tax withholding rather than completing compliance independently. Proactively advanced POB special project initiation, while monitoring project progress to identify overdue risks. Assisted in developing seller interaction and fee standards decisions during the process. This capability was ultimately extended to local products;
- Progressively advanced seller education: GNE compliance standards continuously iterated with complex content, and seller comprehension costs were high. Through data analysis and research, progressively developed phased/staged/timeline/category-specific seller outreach lists and training directions (targeted invite top sellers -> expand invitations -> full rollout; electronics/non-electronics; GPSR/EPR/labels; apparel/non-apparel). Conducted 10 seller training sessions. Enriched outreach methods by type and seller tier (outbound calls/pop-ups/in-app messages/industry 1v1/seller Q&A groups). Produced 5 seller training documents (including key label qualification preparation, German packaging EPR application SOP, basic regulations introduction, seller backend operations training, etc.);
- Industry collaboration and coordination: Aligned initialization targets with industries, built data dashboards, set individual targets, formulated industry buyer special incentives, established seller group POC Q&A system and lagging industry catch-up meeting system to improve industry, buyer, and seller engagement. Simultaneously adjusted external messaging in real-time based on regulatory requirements and internal cadence to encourage sellers to complete compliance qualification preparation as early as possible;
- Supply chain/product coordination: Collaborated with product and supply chain to improve success rates across all stages during final sprint. GNE review success rate increased from 82% to 95%. Products with inventory ratio increased from 50% to 75%+. Daily product recommendation volume increased from 70K to 200K. Completed 460K product listings within 2 days.

