Q2 Project Awards.reason:
[US Tariff Response Initiative]
Situation
The White House announced on April 2 that China-origin goods would no longer receive T86 de minimis exemption starting May 2. Due to volatile policy changes, average import tariff rates on Chinese e-commerce goods shifted four times within a month—from 0% to 75% to 125% to 166% to 55%—causing severe disruption to e-commerce platforms' operations and adaptability.

Task
- Ensure the platform continues normal operations post-tax reform, with no customs clearance bottlenecks and reasonable control of new tax costs and fulfillment cost reduction;
- Control 95th percentile end-to-end delivery time within 15 days.

Action
- Rapidly established cross-team response group; GS merchant flow, cross-border logistics, product/R&D, and legal teams met continuously for 9 weeks with daily task cleanup;
- Tracked Trump administration's volatile policies, adjusted product solutions 3 times, and urgently established new T01 and T11 customs clearance capabilities;
- Monitored competitor dynamics daily;
- Coordinated with treasury, finance, insurance, and other departments to complete platform import IOR qualification applications, customs duty bond purchases, and tax payment account setup;
- Under the new customs clearance model, most platform imported goods involve PGA regulations from over 30 US government departments. Cross-functional teams built product qualification collection and exception handling processes from scratch;
- Anticipated US Customs' stance on multi-package consolidated declarations and established product capability for consolidating $2,500 worth of goods per customs declaration;
- Completed price adjustments on 4/25, initiated T86 order cutoff and warehouse clearance on 4/26, completed final T86 duty-free declaration for last batch of packages by noon on 5/1, switched to T11 customs declaration mode at midnight on 5/2, started first test orders on 5/3, and made collective decision to resume shipping on 5/7;
- Warehouse completed exit and production shift adjustments: Initiated Jiangmen warehouse exit while ensuring future one-year business needs. In terms of production strategy, Huadu warehouse adjusted from 24H production to single shift (eliminated night shift), Labor Day/Dragon Boat Festival shutdown, etc., to achieve cost reduction.

Result
- Successfully completed US tax reform business transition on 5/2 with no business bottlenecks;
- Daily average GMV recovered to $xxxM, with customs duty base reasonably optimized to xx% of sale price;
- Customs declaration fee per package compressed from $2.62 to $0.013;
- US end-to-end 95th percentile delivery time stabilized at approximately 13 days, outperforming competitors;
- Warehouse savings: Jiangmen warehouse exit reduced operating costs by 39.33M RMB—Jiangmen exit achieved annual cost savings of approximately 34.5M RMB (warehouse rent reduced by ~4.26M RMB/month, utilities and transportation reduced by ~0.35M RMB/month) + 4.83M RMB recovered from equipment/materials. To ensure fulfillment experience, Huadu warehouse started single-shift production saving 1.6M RMB/month; warehouse outbound 95th percentile time extended 5-7H without impacting end-to-end delivery time; single-day shutdowns during Labor Day (5/2) and Dragon Boat Festival saved 0.5M RMB.

